& [CoordinatorContract] is deterministic and effectless
  + [coordinator_identity] is cantor-effectless-coordinator/0.1
  + one invocation binds exactly two admitted process definitions to the exact request, catalogue, procedure, IR, admission, schema, anchor, policy, participant, frame, and budget generations
  + stable readiness and semantic identity select at most one process-state transition per scheduler step
  + scheduler logical time is supplied integer state and never a physical clock read
  + local operations remain composable with emit, receive, yield, wait-logical, reactivate, join, return, and fault
  + all outcomes contain exact states, steps, messages, continuation archive, active-continuation pointers, terminal returns, session successor, causal trace, budgets, residuals, and typed output or fault

& [MessageContract] is explicit and causal
  + sender and receiver are named process-definition participants with exact role and permitted message kinds
  + each message binds session, frame generation, SOP anchors, closed kind, declared tag, typed payload, evidence, logical time, causal predecessors, and expiry
  + delivery is deterministic by immutable identity and cannot bypass accepted and emitted tag contracts
  + message and queue exhaustion returns a typed resource refusal

& [ContinuationContract] preserves the walk
  + yield passivates one process and records the exact successor program point as a content-bound SerializedContinuation
  + receive, logical wait, and join also serialize their exact awaited condition and state generation
  + reactivate records a wake request and the scheduler performs a separate exact state transition
  + resumed continuations remain in immutable history while their active pointers are cleared
  + aggregate validation recomputes continuation digests and refuses substitution

& [TokenRingContract] is exact
  + [token_ring_identity] is cantor-token-ring/0.1
  + only the exact current required token holder may pass
  + each pass binds session, frame generation, complete participant set digest, SOP anchor set digest, policy, predecessor pass, participant, and monotonic logical time
  + stable candidate requires every exact required participant once in one complete pass chain over the unchanged frame and policy generation
  + a real semantic frame change increments generation and clears the active pass set
  + silence, absence, duplicated participant, forged digest, stale generation, no-op revision, and out-of-turn pass are not assent

& [ReplayContract] is byte comparable
  + exact immutable inputs are executed twice through the same coordinator
  + outcome digests and complete structured values must match
  + the replay receipt binds invocation, procedure, coordinator, catalogue generation, both outcome digests, match disposition, and its own content digest

& [TruthAndAuthorityBoundary] is permanent
  + deterministic does not mean true
  + stable candidate does not mean admitted, safe, fit, or consented
  + process messages are explicit later-pass context and not shared model hidden state
  + no thread, physical clock, randomness, filesystem, network, database, process, provider, notification, model, persistence, unsafe code, device, external effect, or FPGA surface is present

